assical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:237), also stated in blueprint `def:ld-question-distribution`. Consequently, earlier blocks vanish and later blocks remain untruncated. The implemented lemmas `projX_directPrefixProjection_embZ` and `projZ_directPrefixProjection_embX` correctly prove this. Correct the module\u2019s mathematical description before merge.\n\nThe statement-integrity audit found no newly added proof-debt hypotheses or changed public conclusions. The uniform mixtures and inflation factors `2m` and `4m\u00b2` match the cited estimates. Diagonal resampling preserves the joint line-point law, including zero directions. `exists_subLineWitness` retains its explicitly documented status as a directly indexed auxiliary result; transport to the source carrier remains unresolved.\n\nValidation: the checkout diff matches the authoritative patch; `Lines.lean` and `DiagonalResampling.lean` type-check. All eight principal added or completed results have only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound` in their axiom closures. No new proof holes or bypasses were found. The two pre-existing combined-line construction `sorry`s remain. A full build was not repeated; the supplied CI status is green for the reviewed head.\n",
